# Sample Brain - Project Rule

## Source of truth
- Prefer repository code (`src/`) and tests (`tests/`) over assumptions.
- Keep command examples aligned with `src/cli.py`.
- For the realtime Workbench cluster #318, `docs/REALTIME_WORKBENCH_SCOPE.md` is the canonical product boundary.

## Product boundary
- Offline/local-first means no mandatory cloud processing; it does not prohibit local real-time playback or recording.
- The local Workbench may add shared `TEMPO`, `SYNC`, grid-bound playback, mixing, recording, non-destructive editing and `HÄFTIG`.
- A narrow native audio core may own the hard real-time path; Python/Tkinter remains UI, analysis and control.
- #318 is not a full DAW and does not require a VST/VST3/FL Studio plugin.
- Existing analysis, Track Map, BeatGrid, Deconstruction, Packs and Stem contracts remain valid and must not be redefined as session time.

## Safety
- Never write machine-local paths or secrets into tracked files.
- Never commit private samples, tracks, recordings, generated audio, device dumps or runtime audio caches.
- Preserve graceful fallback behavior for optional embedding backends.

## Change style
- Keep edits scoped and minimal.
- Update tests when behavior changes.
- For schema/data contract changes in `src/db.py`, verify affected pipeline modules (`scan`, `analyze`, `classify`, `embed`, `index`, `search`).
